				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Project): Rename user-data directory root from .land to .fiddee\n\nFollowing the product rebranding to FIDDEE, update the hardcoded user-data directory path from `$HOME/.land` to `$HOME/.fiddee` to align with the new product identity across all TypeScript layers.\n\nKey modifications:\n- **Cocoon**: Extract the path logic into a shared `FiddeeRoot()` atom at `Source/Platform/FiddeeRoot.ts`. Update `Context.ts` and `HostHandler.ts` to use this atom for extension storage, global storage, and logs. Refresh the extension-bug frame matcher in `NotificationHandler.ts`.\n- **Output**: Correct inline documentation and `Why` strings in `Pipeline.ts`, `PluginIndex.ts`, `ExtensionGalleryService.ts`, and the Icon Stylesheet URL rewriter to reference `~/.fiddee/extensions/`.\n- **Wind**: Update the `ResolveConfiguration` comment referencing the recently opened workspaces file path.\n- **Mountain**: Synchronized to the matching HEAD; no functional delta for this specific commit.\n\nRebuild all ESBuild Target artifacts and generated bundles to reflect the new path constants.",
			"SHA": "2482835a24e221d14be55ed2ccfb4cdfb3ec4237"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-19T22:23:31Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				129,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Project): Synchronize Element submodule for workspace save IPC and Wind boot hardening\n\nAdvance the Element submodule from 504dc46b to bbd041b6, wiring the full workspace save round-trip (Cocoon -> Mountain -> Sky) and fixing two Tauri IPC fallback crash sources in Wind at boot.\n\nKey modifications:\n- **Mountain**: Add three new IPC handler arms to the Workspace dispatch table — `Workspace.Save`, `Workspace.SaveAs`, and `Workspace.SaveAll` (including the legacy `saveAll` method name used by gRPC/Client.ts). All three degrade gracefully when Sky has no handler registered, logging a warning and returning the original URI or null instead of crashing the extension host.\n- **Cocoon**: Rebuild all 39 ESBuild Target bundles and regenerate the RouteManifest, raising the Mountain RPC method count from 130 to 134 with a generation timestamp of 2026-05-19T22:15:03Z.\n- **Wind**: Fix two boot-time crash sources in `ResolveConfiguration` — (1) add `__TAURI_INTERNALS__?.invoke` to the fallback chain before the `__TAURI__` variants so the Tauri IPC bridge resolves in Tauri v2 webview contexts; (2) replace all `|| undefined` path fallbacks (homeDir, tmpDir, userDataDir, logsPath) with concrete defaults so `path.posix.join(undefined, 'User')` no longer throws during workbench initialisation.\n\nTogether these changes complete the `vscode.workspace.save()`/`saveAll()`/`saveAs()` IPC round-trip for extensions while hardening Wind against Tauri version mismatches and missing IPC responses at startup.",
			"SHA": "5757696ff078d272771b17a9f39d4359a9df2797"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-19T21:54:00Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				129,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Project): Synchronize Element submodule for active editor tracking and OS property caching\n\nAdvance the Element submodule from a433ff65 to 504dc46b, wiring synchronous active editor tracking in Cocoon and caching OS property queries in Mountain.\n\nKey modifications across components:\n- **Cocoon**: Wire `window.didChangeActiveTextEditor` from Handler.ts into a minimal TextEditor stub derived from URI and languageId. Patch `__activeTextEditor` on Context so extensions reading `vscode.window.activeTextEditor` synchronously in `activate()` see the current value. Upgrade `showTextDocument` from a fire-and-forget notification to a `sendRequest` round-trip returning the TextEditor stub from Mountain, with a disposable fallback to prevent crashes when chaining `.selection` or `.revealRange`. Migrate `ExtensionSecretStorage` from `sendNotification` to `sendRequest` with namespaced methods (`secrets.get`, `secrets.store`, `secrets.delete`) and scoped `extensionId` isolation.\n- **Mountain**: Cache OS property collection (type, release, arch, CPU topology) and Rosetta 2 detection behind `OnceLock`, eliminating ~10ms subprocess overhead per IPC call. After document open, call `SetActiveDocumentURI` on application state and fire a fire-and-forget gRPC `window.didChangeActiveTextEditor` notification to keep Cocoon's shim in sync. Refactor `localPty:getTerminalLayoutInfo`/`setTerminalLayoutInfo` to use `GetStorageValue`/`UpdateStorageValue` on StorageProvider, removing manual JSON serialization.\n\nTogether these changes eliminate three extension-host crash categories (synchronous reads of undefined `activeTextEditor`, awaited `showTextDocument` returning undefined, and unhandled secret storage notification rejections) while reducing IPC latency for OS queries and keeping terminal layout persistence simpler.",
			"SHA": "411b4d6b8240fff16cd87885420d4904ecaf3270"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-19T21:47:35Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				129,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Synchronize Element submodules for terminal persistence and dependency updates\n\nAdvance the Element submodule from b0d4545a to a433ff65, integrating terminal layout state persistence, native color scheme caching, and dependency alignment across Cocoon, Mountain, Output, and Sky.\n\nKey modifications:\n- **Mountain**: Wire `localPty:getTerminalLayoutInfo` and `setTerminalLayoutInfo` to `StorageProvider` to restore active terminal tabs and dimensions after window reloads. Cache native color scheme detection in a `OnceLock` to eliminate repeated OS syscalls during boot.\n- **Cocoon**: Update `@types/node` to 25.9.1 and `protobufjs` to 8.4.0 via Dependabot.\n- **Output**: Normalize case-statement indentation in `Run.sh` and `prepublishOnly.sh` to consistent 0-tab/1-tab formatting.\n- **Sky**: Bump `@astrojs/ts-plugin` to 1.10.9 and `astro` to 6.3.5 via Dependabot.\n\nThese changes ensure terminal state survives workbench reloads, reduce startup latency, and align all dependencies with upstream releases.",
			"SHA": "289329062931b417680b41819b25b7b5981f8086"
		}
	],
